{"id":"son-of-man","title":"Son of Man","kind":"title","en":["Son of man"],"la":["Filius hominis","Filium hominis","Filii hominis","Filio hominis"],"gist":"In the Gospels this is the title Jesus most often uses of himself. In the Old Testament the phrase can simply mean 'a human being' (God addresses Ezekiel this way again and again), but in Daniel 7 'one like a son of man' comes with the clouds of heaven and receives everlasting rule from the Ancient of Days. Jesus draws on both: he is truly one of us, and he is the figure who judges and reigns.","original":"Hebrew ben adam; Aramaic bar enash in Daniel 7:13; Greek ho huios tou anthropou. The Greek phrase is unusual, which suggests it reproduces a Semitic idiom.","passages":[{"ref":"Daniel 7:13-14","note":"The vision of one like a son of man receiving dominion."},{"ref":"Ezekiel 2:1","note":"God addresses the prophet as 'son of man', the first of many times."},{"ref":"Psalm 8:4","note":"'What is man... or the son of man that you care for him?'"},{"ref":"Mark 2:10","note":"'The Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins.'"},{"ref":"Mark 14:62","note":"Before the high priest Jesus joins his own words to Daniel 7."},{"ref":"Matthew 8:20","note":"'The Son of man hath not where to lay his head.'"}],"related":["son-of-god","ancient-of-days","kingdom"],"total":209,"byBook":{"1CH":2,"1KI":1,"2KI":1,"ACT":1,"DAN":3,"DEU":1,"EZK":93,"GEN":1,"HEB":1,"ISA":2,"JDT":2,"JER":4,"JHN":11,"JOB":3,"JOS":2,"LUK":26,"MAT":29,"MRK":13,"NUM":6,"PSA":4,"REV":2,"SIR":1},"verses":["1CH.7.14","1CH.7.17","1KI.4.13","2KI.15.23","ACT.7.55","DAN.7.13","DAN.8.17","DAN.10.16","DEU.3.14","EZK.2.1","EZK.2.3","EZK.2.6","EZK.2.8","EZK.3.1","EZK.3.3","EZK.3.4","EZK.3.10","EZK.3.17","EZK.3.25","EZK.4.1","EZK.4.16","EZK.5.1","EZK.6.2","EZK.7.2","EZK.8.5","EZK.8.6","EZK.8.8","EZK.8.12","EZK.8.15","EZK.8.17","EZK.11.2","EZK.11.4","EZK.11.15","EZK.12.2","EZK.12.3","EZK.12.9","EZK.12.18","EZK.12.22","EZK.12.27","EZK.13.2","EZK.13.17","EZK.14.3","EZK.14.13